DTSTART:20260701T130000Z
DTEND:20260701T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Flora Field Day at 9:00 a.m.\n\n•    Sign up for this session
  at tinyurl.com/florafielddays \n•    Registration required by June 29.\
 n•    Free\; recommended for ages 12 and up.\n•    Session location: A
 llens Creek SRA\n\nWant to work on your flora identification skills? Pract
 ice with a naturalist! Field day emphasis is on proper use and application
  of an ID key\, which opens the door to identifying thousands of species. 
 The naturalist will work with each attendee based on their prior experienc
 e. If you’ve never worked with flower ID before\, this is a great way to
  learn. If you have prior experience\, this is a fun way to practice your 
 skills (and maybe add some new blooms to your life list!). 2 hours\n\nThin
 gs to Bring:\n•    Newcomb’s Wildflower Guide (extra copies available\
 , if you don’t have your own)\n•    bug spray (long pants are also a g
 ood idea!)\n•    hat and sunglasses (for sun protection)\n•    water b
 ottle (pre-filled)\n•    camera (if you’re the picture-taking type)
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Allens Creek SRA (Allens Creek Road\, Bloomington)
SUMMARY:Flora Field Day\, Allens Creek SRA (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/flora-field-day-allens-creek-sra-
 monroe-lake-2572
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
