BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20260721T033021Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53312039799863
DTSTART:20260823T223000Z
DTEND:20260823T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Explore Monroe Paddling Trip at 6:30 p.m.\n\nRegistration requi
 red by August 20.Trip fee is $15 per person.Limited to 10 people. Restrict
 ed to ages 16 and up. All participants must have at least 2 hours of prior
  paddling experience OR have completed one of our Beginner Kayaking worksh
 ops.Bring your own canoe/kayak\, or rent a sit-on-top kayak (weight limit:
  275 pounds) for an additional $20.Location: Northfork of Salt Creek\n\nEx
 plore the quieter side of Monroe Lake during these guided paddling trips t
 hat journey through backwaters\, wetlands\, bays\, and/or slow-moving stre
 ams. Trips highlight beautiful views\, hidden wildlife\, aquatic plants\, 
 and unique land features. Find your new favorite place to kayak! 2 hours \
 n\n \n\nREFUND/TRANSFER/CANCELLATION POLICY\n\nRegistrations are considere
 d final and no refunds or date transfers are available\, with limited exce
 ptions. You may transfer a registration(s) to another person(s) by contact
 ing Jill Vance at jvance@dnr.IN.gov from the same email used in your origi
 nal registration. Provide the name(s) and email(s) of the person to whom y
 ou want to transfer the registration(s). Requests must be received at leas
 t 48 hours prior to the start of the workshop.In the event that the trip i
 s cancelled by the instructor for weather\, low registration\, or instruct
 or illness\, registered participants may opt to transfer their registratio
 n to another Explore Monroe trip on a different date or receive a full ref
 und. Weather Cancellation Policy: If only light rain is anticipated\, the 
 trip will likely proceed as scheduled. However\, if there is a strong poss
 ibility (as determined by the instructor) of moderate to heavy rain\, high
  winds\, or thunder/lightning\, the workshop will be cancelled for safety 
 reasons. Any decision to cancel due to anticipated weather will be made at
  least 2 hours prior to the trip start time. In the event of a cancellatio
 n\, an email notice will be sent to all registrants.Low Registration Polic
 y: The trip may be cancelled\, at the discretion of the instructor\, if th
 ere are fewer than 3 people signed up by the registration deadline. If the
  trip is cancelled due to low registration\, all participants will be noti
 fied within 24 hours of the close of registration.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Northfork of Salt Creek (directions emailed to regis
 trants prior to trip)
SUMMARY:Explore Monroe Paddling Trip\, Northfork of Salt Creek (Monroe Lake
 )
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/explore-monroe-paddling-trip-nort
 hfork-of-salt-creek-monroe-lake-9481
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20260721T033021Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53312249612394
DTSTART:20260824T223000Z
DTEND:20260824T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:WINGS: Intro to Kayaking\n\nPart 1 on Monday\, August 24 at 6:3
 0 p.m. (2.5 hours)\nPart 2 on Wednesday\, August 26 at 6:30 p.m. (2 hours)
 \n\nInstructor: Jill Vance\, Monroe Lake Interpretive NaturalistLocation: 
 Monroe Lake in Bloomington (Part 1 at Cutright SRA\, Part 2 at Pinegrove S
 RA)Fee: $40 per person (includes kayak\, paddle\, and PFD for both days)Re
 strictions: Limited to 8 women\, ages 16+ only. Kayaks have a weight limit
  of 275 pounds.Registration Window: Opens July 24 and closes August 20 (or
  when all spots are full).Registration Instructions: Registration is restr
 icted to people with the promo code. Select "Register" and then scroll dow
 n to the bottom of the pop-up window to enter the promo code and hit "Appl
 y promo." This will unlock the registration.If you love seeing wildlife\, 
 or just enjoy exploring\, kayaking is for you! This two-part workshop is s
 pecifically designed for beginners with zero (or very little) paddling exp
 erience. \n\nDuring Part 1\, we’ll cover boating safety\, discuss the ty
 pes of kayaks and their pros/cons\, and teach basic kayaking and paddling 
 skills. This session will conclude with supervised paddling time in a quie
 t water area to practice. During Part 2\, we’ll enjoy a relaxing paddle 
 together into a backwater area to enjoy the sights and sounds of nature! \
 n\nWhen you register\, you are signing up for BOTH parts. Please note that
  attendance and full participation in Part 1 is required to attend Part 2.
 \n\nBACKUP DATES are August 28 and 30. Please hold these dates in your cal
 endar as well\, in case one or both parts of the workshop must be reschedu
 led due to weather or instructor illness.\n\nThis is an official WINGS eve
 nt! The goal of Women in Nature Gaining Skills (WINGS) is to encourage and
  empower women with the skills and confidence they need to partake in outd
 oor recreation activities in the south-central Indiana area. Each WINGS ev
 ent features women-led hands-on training\, with the goal of building a com
 munity of women interested in outdoor recreation. WINGS events are open to
  women ages 16 and up.\n \n\nREFUND/TRANSFER/CANCELLATION POLICY\n\nRegist
 rations are considered final and no refunds or date transfers are availabl
 e\, with limited exceptions. In the event that either part of the workshop
  is cancelled by the instructor for weather or instructor illness\, we wil
 l reschedule for a backup date. BACKUP DATES are August 28 and 30. You may
  transfer a registration(s) to another person(s) by contacting Jill Vance 
 at jvance@dnr.IN.gov from the same email used in your original registratio
 n. Provide the name(s) and email(s) of the person to whom you want to tran
 sfer the registration(s). Requests must be received at least 48 hours prio
 r to the start of the workshop.Weather Cancellation Policy: If only light 
 rain is anticipated\, the trip will likely proceed as scheduled. However\,
  if there is a strong possibility (as determined by the instructor) of mod
 erate to heavy rain\, high winds\, or thunder/lightning\, the workshop wil
 l be cancelled for safety reasons. Any decision to cancel due to anticipat
 ed weather will be made at least 2 hours prior to the trip start time. In 
 the event of a cancellation\, an email notice will be sent to all registra
 nts.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Cutright SRA (Part 1) and Pinegrove (Part 2) -- dire
 ctions will be emailed after registration closes
SUMMARY:WINGS: Intro to Kayaking (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/wings-intro-to-kayaking-monroe-la
 ke
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
